  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "Intel finished at nearly ten times its starting value, and Microsoft at about six times. Disney and both broad share baskets also gained. The window ends in August 2000; changes after that date are outside this result. One five-year period is only a slice of history.\n\nThe years ahead brought Pathfinder to Mars and a rescue of the investment fund Long-Term Capital Management after heavy losses. The euro began as a shared currency for financial transactions in 1999. Notes and coins came later. Scientific advances and financial trouble happened in the same period; the world did not follow a single upbeat or gloomy story.\n\nThe ending date matters. A gain measured through August 2000 says nothing by itself about money invested for longer or bought at a different price. Look at the full path and ask how you would have felt during its setbacks. A stock can finish with a large gain without giving its owner a smooth five years.",
    "source_ids": [
      "french-us",
      "french-international",
      "fred-gs5",
      "yahoo-msft",
      "yahoo-dis",
      "yahoo-intc",
